From 02d4e80b73cb4c5e622227ef91f9522637d265b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VTS port <vts-port@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 22:50:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(project): sidecar subtitles, source sections, and cue
 remapping

Three pure modules, no I/O and no engine type in any signature, so a cue
list can be read, cut, moved and written back with no project open and no
media on disk.

subtitle: SubRip and WebVTT in and out. One tolerant pass reads both,
because they differ in their header and their decimal mark and in almost
nothing else - a byte-order mark, CRLF, cue indices, a WEBVTT header
carrying a title, NOTE/STYLE/REGION blocks, cue settings trailing the
timing line, inline tags, and an MM:SS.mmm stamp with the hours left off
all arrive in real files. Word timings do not survive this format, which
is why captionmap exists.

sections: the arithmetic a trim by content is made of. silence_spans
reads the lines an FFmpeg silencedetect filter prints, including the last
pause of a recording, which never prints its end; merge folds overlaps
and adjacencies and can keep a pad of air at both ends of every cut;
complement returns the kept ranges, which is the whole of a trim; and
build_sections tiles the source into caption/silence/other pieces so what
is about to be deleted can be read first. Boundaries come from both sets,
so no piece is half silence and half speech.

captionmap: a cue's words, and what a cut does to them. clean_words puts
a recogniser's output into the shape everything downstream assumes -
sorted, inside the cue, never overlapping a neighbour, punctuation riding
on the word before it rather than standing alone - in any script, since
the question is is_alphanumeric and not is_ascii_alphanumeric. remap
moves a cue list through a cut: shifted by everything removed ahead of
it, split where a cut went through one, joined again where the halves of
one sentence landed back to back, gone where nothing was kept. The words
travel with their cue and are clipped at the cut with it, so a reveal on
the far side of a trim still lights the word being heard.

215 tests in the crate, 101 of them new.

Signed-off-by: VTS port <vts-port@local>
